WEBVTT

00:01.810 --> 00:06.510
<i>There once was a powerless prince who 
saved a kingdom with his tiny courage.</i>

00:07.610 --> 00:10.090
<i>The courage to face challenges...</i>

00:10.090 --> 00:12.120
<i>The courage to never give up...</i>

00:12.470 --> 00:14.680
<i>The courage to trust others...</i>

00:15.430 --> 00:20.080
<i>A treasure chest of untold courage 
is now about to be opened.</i>

00:27.130 --> 00:33.550
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

00:27.130 --> 00:33.550
<b>— The Treasure Chest of Courage —</b>

01:53.040 --> 01:56.960
<i>Bojji, who lost his throne to his 
brother, Daida, had gone on a journey.</i>

01:57.530 --> 01:59.540
<i>In order to become a mighty man,</i>

01:59.850 --> 02:02.190
<i>he became the apprentice of 
Despa of the Underworld.</i>

02:03.000 --> 02:07.110
<i>With Kage's support, his training 
was making good progress.</i>

02:07.430 --> 02:09.430
<i>Or at least it should have been...</i>

02:10.600 --> 02:14.900
<b>Kage's Errand</b>

02:12.760 --> 02:15.310
I think we're ready to go and get Despa.

02:15.810 --> 02:18.590
Whoa! What's all that?

02:18.590 --> 02:21.910
Bojji, Despa is yelling 
about something. Let's go.

02:23.050 --> 02:25.150
What's the matter, Despa?

02:27.860 --> 02:30.710
Just look at this. Right here.

02:31.120 --> 02:31.870
Right here!

02:35.850 --> 02:37.200
Is there something stuck on there?

02:37.730 --> 02:41.960
It's an age spot! An age spot! And on
 my handsome face! An <i>age</i> spot!

02:43.910 --> 02:46.110
Everybody gets those, right?

02:46.340 --> 02:49.600
Others may get them, but <i>I</i> do not!

02:50.430 --> 02:52.850
I cannot be getting one!

02:54.380 --> 02:59.640
I can no longer provide training to Bojji.

02:59.640 --> 03:01.810
Huh?! Why not?!

03:01.810 --> 03:04.580
You said you were gonna make 
Bojji stronger, remember?!

03:05.640 --> 03:08.290
Perhaps I haven't been getting enough sleep.

03:10.510 --> 03:11.960
I'm going back to bed.

03:12.820 --> 03:16.140
Huh?! What about training?!

03:16.140 --> 03:19.840
I told you, now isn't the time for that.

03:19.840 --> 03:24.040
Ah, I've had it. I can't take a single 
step out of the room looking like this.

03:24.040 --> 03:28.320
Don't talk like that! Isn't there some 
kind of medicine that fixes age spots?

03:28.320 --> 03:29.880
I'll go buy it for you.

03:30.980 --> 03:34.210
Look, I've heard that meat 
and veggies and... you know,

03:34.210 --> 03:36.980
fruits are good for your looks!

03:39.870 --> 03:41.180
You're right! That's it!

03:42.460 --> 03:46.490
That's it! There's always the shuddercap!

03:46.490 --> 03:47.820
The shuddercap?

03:48.150 --> 03:51.340
It's a mushroom that's very 
effective for preserving beauty.

03:51.340 --> 03:52.820
If I ate one of those...

03:53.470 --> 03:56.430
my skin's beauty would be revived.

03:56.430 --> 03:57.420
In theory!

04:00.550 --> 04:04.030
Kage, take this and go buy me 
a shuddercap, if you would.

04:04.560 --> 04:05.260
You bet!

04:05.530 --> 04:07.960
Then you have to train Bojji!

04:07.960 --> 04:09.040
Huh?

04:09.040 --> 04:11.290
Hmm, I suppose I do.

04:11.770 --> 04:13.250
Well, shall we get to it?

04:14.740 --> 04:17.890
A shuddercap... A shuddercap...

04:17.890 --> 04:20.280
Where exactly are they?

04:22.190 --> 04:25.070
Mister! Got a shuddercap?

04:25.070 --> 04:28.570
I don't have a mushroom that rare.

04:28.570 --> 04:29.740
You, either?

04:29.740 --> 04:33.410
Ah, man! How come I can't 
find one anywhere?!

04:33.410 --> 04:35.050
Give it up.

04:35.050 --> 04:37.940
It's not every day you see 
one of <i>those</i> in a store.

04:37.940 --> 04:41.370
It's not all that easy to pick a shuddercap.

04:41.750 --> 04:44.610
If you head one hill over that 
way to the Okkana Forest,

04:44.610 --> 04:46.610
you can find some shuddercaps.

04:46.610 --> 04:50.750
But there's a creature in that forest 
that's downright terrifying.

04:50.750 --> 04:55.120
If you get caught, you're done for. 
It's not very easy to get away.

04:57.420 --> 05:00.390
<i>This is for Bojji. 
There's no choice but to go.</i>

05:11.350 --> 05:15.940
Please, pay me no mind. Sunlight is
 one of the causes of age spots.

05:15.940 --> 05:18.580
Even down here in the underworld, 
where you can't see the sun,

05:18.580 --> 05:20.140
you can't be too careful!

05:24.270 --> 05:27.590
If he catches me, I'm done for?
 Who is this guy?

05:29.220 --> 05:30.010
Eep!

05:37.210 --> 05:40.010
Wah! Don't scare me like that!

05:47.380 --> 05:48.310
What's that?

05:49.620 --> 05:50.760
What is it?

05:51.690 --> 05:53.050
What is it?!

05:55.820 --> 05:57.160
It's here!

06:03.510 --> 06:07.010
Oh, no! What do I do?!

06:39.300 --> 06:41.690
<i>Was </i>that<i> the downright terrifying guy?</i>

06:41.690 --> 06:44.240
He's right. If I got caught, 
I'd definitely get eaten.

06:45.640 --> 06:47.510
Old lady, are you okay?

06:47.510 --> 06:51.650
Yeah, thank you. I'm still alive,
 thanks to you.

06:51.650 --> 06:53.150
It's all good.

06:53.150 --> 06:57.040
Say, would you know where mushrooms 
called shuddercaps grow?

06:57.040 --> 06:59.940
Well, you're sure making a tall order.

07:00.410 --> 07:02.960
I'm sorry, but I couldn't say.

07:02.960 --> 07:04.270
No, huh?

07:05.570 --> 07:06.690
Oh, dear.

07:06.690 --> 07:09.530
Oh, you must have broken it earlier.

07:09.530 --> 07:11.190
Sorry, but I need to get moving.

07:11.480 --> 07:17.510
Yow-ow-ow-ow... I think I must 
have sprained my ankle. Yowch...

07:17.510 --> 07:19.650
We can't have that, can we?

07:22.160 --> 07:23.830
Well, I'll be going now.

07:24.610 --> 07:29.880
Oh, what am I going to do? I can't 
clean with my ankle like this.

07:29.880 --> 07:31.410
And my throat is sore, too.

07:31.410 --> 07:35.610
I'm liable to get buried under 
all this dust and die here.

07:37.390 --> 07:40.770
Okay, fine! I'll clean up for you!

07:40.770 --> 07:43.610
Oh, you will? How helpful of you.

07:52.750 --> 07:55.000
You're so good at this.

07:55.000 --> 07:57.050
The room is sparkling.

07:57.050 --> 07:58.810
I-It's no big deal.

07:58.810 --> 08:00.720
If you're this good at cleaning,

08:00.720 --> 08:03.410
I'm sure you must be a whiz at laundry, too.

08:03.410 --> 08:06.000
You could say that. It's a cinch for me.

08:06.320 --> 08:10.660
Whoo! I got those nice and clean,
 if I do say so myself.

08:10.660 --> 08:14.120
Huh? What am I doing all this for, anyway?

08:14.560 --> 08:19.820
Old lady, the laundry is done! I need 
to get going to find those mushrooms.

08:19.820 --> 08:22.470
You do? Then I'll see you out.

08:22.470 --> 08:24.780
Whoa! Are you all right?

08:25.500 --> 08:30.790
Poor pitiful me. I can't plant the 
seedlings I bought in this condition.

08:30.790 --> 08:31.220
Huh?

08:31.220 --> 08:33.860
Oh, it's so chilly today.

08:34.290 --> 08:37.070
That's the last log of firewood, too.

08:37.070 --> 08:39.570
Once that's burned up,

08:39.570 --> 08:43.210
I'll probably just freeze to death.

08:43.770 --> 08:47.390
Aw, man! I'll take care 
of <i>all</i> of it for you!

09:18.570 --> 09:21.540
I figured that as long as I was at it,

09:21.540 --> 09:24.490
covering myself up entirely 
would be more effective.

09:24.490 --> 09:27.130
I stacked plenty of firewood for you.

09:27.130 --> 09:29.040
And I folded your laundry.

09:29.780 --> 09:31.850
That should do it, right?

09:31.850 --> 09:34.510
I suppose so. One last thing...

09:34.510 --> 09:37.640
Would you mind doing something about this?

09:37.640 --> 09:41.370
Hmm, that's something 
I can't help you with. Sorry.

09:41.370 --> 09:42.490
I see.

09:42.490 --> 09:46.790
Okay, I have to get going. I have 
to hurry and find a shuddercap.

09:46.790 --> 09:49.940
Right this minute? 
That's out of the question.

09:50.320 --> 09:52.430
It's too dark out.

09:52.780 --> 09:54.010
Oh, no.

09:54.490 --> 09:57.800
It's too bad it didn't pan out for you.

09:57.800 --> 09:59.580
<i>What</i> didn't pan out?

09:59.580 --> 10:04.410
You're trying to pick shuddercaps to 
sell for a good price in town, right?

10:04.410 --> 10:06.920
That's not what I'm doing! I...

10:07.960 --> 10:11.160
wanted to bring one home 
with me for a friend.

10:11.430 --> 10:16.020
Is that so? You really 
<i>are</i> a pushover, huh?

10:16.800 --> 10:19.930
See you. Be sure to take it easy, now.

10:21.560 --> 10:23.510
Just a moment!

10:25.410 --> 10:28.010
I baked too much pie.

10:28.010 --> 10:29.960
Here, take this home with you.

10:29.960 --> 10:31.750
Th-Thanks.

10:32.880 --> 10:34.150
Later.

10:36.110 --> 10:40.080
Huh? I thought the old lady hurt her ankle.

10:40.930 --> 10:42.250
Oh well.

10:44.020 --> 10:45.580
I'm back.

10:45.580 --> 10:47.440
Well, you sure took your time.

10:49.130 --> 10:51.830
So, did you get a shuddercap?

10:51.830 --> 10:56.190
Well, the thing is, I looked all over town,
 but nobody was selling them.

10:56.190 --> 10:57.770
I see.

10:57.770 --> 11:00.150
I even went to Okkana Forest to pick one.

11:00.150 --> 11:02.190
Huh? Not <i>that</i> forest!

11:02.190 --> 11:05.500
Anyhow, I ran into an old lady being 
attacked by a wild animal there.

11:05.920 --> 11:10.470
I was helping her around her house, 
and now it's so late. Sorry.

11:12.760 --> 11:15.740
Here's the money you gave me.
 You can have it back.

11:19.820 --> 11:22.090
I smell something good.

11:22.090 --> 11:26.380
Ah, on my way back, the old 
lady let me have this pie.

11:26.380 --> 11:30.670
What a delicate fragrance 
gently wafting into my nose!

11:30.670 --> 11:32.840
There's no question, this is...

11:32.840 --> 11:35.650
a shuddercap pie, isn't it?!

11:35.650 --> 11:36.790
Huh?!

11:36.790 --> 11:41.280
Imagine, that old woman 
giving someone shuddercaps.

11:41.280 --> 11:46.790
Harvesting shuddercaps is dangerous, 
so only a few people can do it.

11:46.790 --> 11:48.150
Dangerous how?

11:48.450 --> 11:52.610
Shuddercaps only grow on the 
backs of wild animals, you see.

11:52.610 --> 11:53.270
Huh?!

11:53.920 --> 11:58.860
And that old woman is famous for taking 
people who are after shuddercaps

11:58.860 --> 12:01.750
and then bossing them around.

12:02.140 --> 12:06.640
<i>If you get caught, you're done for. 
It's not very easy to get away.</i>

12:07.300 --> 12:09.390
So that's what he meant.

12:10.750 --> 12:14.930
All right, allow me to purchase 
these shuddercaps from you now.

12:14.930 --> 12:17.140
Huh? Huh? You mean it?

12:17.140 --> 12:20.760
Well, you <i>did</i> bring them 
back with you, after all.

12:20.760 --> 12:22.980
Wow!

12:26.210 --> 12:28.780
You wonder if there's something I want?

12:34.100 --> 12:35.180
Maybe.

12:39.430 --> 12:40.580
Well, then...

12:41.430 --> 12:43.590
Let's eat!

12:44.860 --> 12:44.950
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

12:44.950 --> 12:45.030
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

12:45.030 --> 12:45.160
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

12:45.160 --> 12:49.870
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

12:49.870 --> 12:53.160
<b>The Prince and Money</b>

12:51.340 --> 12:53.780
<i>Now that the training had resumed,</i>

12:54.560 --> 12:56.910
<i>Bojji and Kage could 
breathe a little easier.</i>

12:58.280 --> 13:00.410
<i>However, all the same,</i>

13:00.960 --> 13:03.930
<i>Despa was still a money-grubbing man.</i>

13:04.880 --> 13:06.170
I'm short.

13:06.940 --> 13:08.260
This is...

13:09.190 --> 13:10.600
not nearly enough!

13:15.770 --> 13:16.520
Today,

13:16.860 --> 13:19.350
I'll need the two of you 
to earn some money.

13:19.350 --> 13:20.150
Wha—?!

13:20.430 --> 13:23.830
Where did this come from?! 
We're here for training—

13:24.880 --> 13:27.790
Bojji is royalty, and ignorant 
of the ways of the world.

13:27.790 --> 13:30.110
He needs to learn about society.

13:30.110 --> 13:33.030
Especially if he wants 
to become a fine king!

13:33.960 --> 13:35.120
I get it.

13:35.120 --> 13:36.010
Besides,

13:36.010 --> 13:39.680
the amount of money you brought 
me is not going to cut it.

13:39.680 --> 13:40.580
Not even close!

13:40.940 --> 13:43.290
It's not worth my while!

13:45.150 --> 13:49.150
It turns out that Despa really is 
all about the money, huh, Bojji?

13:50.470 --> 13:53.560
Hm? You're looking forward to working?

13:55.640 --> 13:58.690
Bojji, what kind of work do you wanna do?

14:00.030 --> 14:01.850
You wanna try all kinds?

14:02.200 --> 14:04.970
Hmm... the thing is...

14:06.380 --> 14:09.210
"Help wanted." A flower shop, eh?

14:09.210 --> 14:11.830
Bojji, you like flowers, 
so this looks okay, doesn't it?

14:13.170 --> 14:16.870
Okay, would you carry these 
flowers into the shop for me?

14:16.870 --> 14:18.340
<i>All</i> of them?!

14:18.340 --> 14:21.240
That's right, if you would.

14:21.240 --> 14:23.940
All right, let's go ahead 
and finish this up quick.

14:30.590 --> 14:32.130
Bojji, are you okay?

14:34.490 --> 14:38.130
Hey there, can't you lift even that?

14:38.130 --> 14:41.490
Everything's fine! I'll work 
double to make up for him!

14:41.490 --> 14:44.220
They're going to wither if 
you take that much time.

14:44.560 --> 14:46.930
Why don't you go find some other work?

14:46.930 --> 14:50.830
There are tons of other jobs 
out there. We'll find one soon.

14:51.950 --> 14:55.060
A restaurant, huh? How about this place?

14:55.900 --> 14:58.880
Hey! Hey!

14:59.320 --> 15:02.900
I'm ready to order! Hey! Hey!

15:02.900 --> 15:06.130
Hey, there's a customer calling you!
 Hurry on over there!

15:07.440 --> 15:09.590
Didn't you hear me?! Hey!

15:09.590 --> 15:13.430
Whoa, just a minute! I'm on my way!

15:14.500 --> 15:17.030
I'm talking to you!

15:17.030 --> 15:19.310
Wah! Hold up! Hold up!

15:19.830 --> 15:21.630
Bojji can't hear anything.

15:21.630 --> 15:22.700
He what?

15:22.700 --> 15:25.540
But he's able to read lips, 
so he can take orders—

15:25.540 --> 15:27.850
He can't work like that!

15:28.580 --> 15:32.280
Don't worry about it. We're not 
gonna let this get us down, right?

15:34.360 --> 15:35.830
Hey, cheer up.

15:36.960 --> 15:40.650
<i>Hmm, what kind of job should 
we try next? There must be...</i>

15:41.790 --> 15:45.130
Damn it! I'll hit it next time, though!

15:58.710 --> 16:00.770
I know! This is it!

16:01.260 --> 16:04.200
Hey, you there! Mister! Ma'am!

16:04.200 --> 16:07.590
If you can hit this guy with 
a beanbag, you get 100 gold coins!

16:07.590 --> 16:10.890
You can't win if you don't try! 
First come, first served!

16:10.890 --> 16:13.290
You're not pulling our legs, right?

16:13.290 --> 16:15.990
We really just have to hit that guy?

16:16.270 --> 16:19.770
It's true. If you can hit him with 
a beanbag from this distance,

16:19.770 --> 16:21.000
you get 100 gold coins!

16:21.000 --> 16:24.700
It only costs ten copper coins 
per throw. What do you say?

16:24.700 --> 16:27.660
Oh yeah! I'm in!

16:30.350 --> 16:31.620
Whoo!

16:32.060 --> 16:34.400
Okay, don't step over those stones, now.

16:34.400 --> 16:36.890
Heh-heh, I'm gonna clock him.

16:45.710 --> 16:46.870
One more throw!

16:47.270 --> 16:48.430
You got it.

16:58.460 --> 16:59.710
It's no use.

16:59.710 --> 17:01.660
We couldn't hit him for anything.

17:04.230 --> 17:08.430
Bojji, look at this! This should 
make Despa happy, right?

17:09.600 --> 17:11.400
Hmm? What is it?

17:13.130 --> 17:16.790
This is all the money I have. I want to try.

17:21.530 --> 17:23.280
Don't do it. Don't do it!

17:23.280 --> 17:25.970
This is just for fun. 
Don't take it seriously.

17:25.970 --> 17:27.910
Young lady, don't do it.

17:27.910 --> 17:29.570
You can't hit him.

17:29.570 --> 17:32.230
Never mind! I want to try, so I will!

17:36.050 --> 17:37.820
Bojji, come here a second.

17:39.030 --> 17:41.830
You can't let her hit you on purpose!

17:41.830 --> 17:44.130
This is what being ignorant 
of the world means.

17:44.130 --> 17:46.340
Look here! Don't let yourself be fooled!

17:47.690 --> 17:49.630
Is she really going through with it?

17:50.500 --> 17:52.010
Okay, here's three throws.

17:53.110 --> 17:54.370
Thank you!

17:54.370 --> 17:55.740
First throw!

17:55.740 --> 17:57.220
Good luck!

17:57.220 --> 17:59.400
Let him have it!

18:05.650 --> 18:09.640
A-At least get it to him. Second throw!

18:13.790 --> 18:15.350
That one was a wild pitch!

18:16.250 --> 18:19.060
Whatever happens, this is 
the last throw, understand?

18:33.120 --> 18:35.300
Oh, she's got him!

18:35.300 --> 18:36.930
Oh, she made it!

18:36.930 --> 18:38.010
Let's see!

18:39.030 --> 18:39.960
Bojji!

18:43.120 --> 18:44.900
Aw...

18:45.650 --> 18:46.670
Too bad.

18:48.080 --> 18:50.020
What? You're done.

18:52.240 --> 18:53.660
That poor girl...

18:53.660 --> 18:57.920
That <i>dumb</i> girl. Poor people 
shouldn't gamble.

18:59.180 --> 19:00.860
H-Hey, Bojji!

19:01.980 --> 19:06.690
I'm sorry, Mom. I wanted 
to buy medicine for you.

19:06.690 --> 19:09.400
You're a silly little girl, you know that?

19:09.630 --> 19:12.470
Hmph, I figured it was something like this.

19:13.540 --> 19:17.120
At the end of the day, 
you're on your own to survive.

19:17.120 --> 19:19.590
You've gotta make your own way.

19:26.020 --> 19:27.600
What are you looking at me like that for?

19:27.990 --> 19:30.160
Do you have something you wanna say?

19:32.000 --> 19:35.150
You think you should have 
let her hit you after all?

19:35.550 --> 19:38.210
Bojji, are you really sure about that?

19:38.210 --> 19:40.310
If she learns that it's easy to make money,

19:40.310 --> 19:42.900
she's the one who's going 
to suffer down the road.

19:44.350 --> 19:47.550
Ah, I see you're back.

19:48.870 --> 19:51.780
How did it go? Did you earn any money?

19:51.780 --> 19:54.740
Th-This is amazing! You made this much?!

19:55.090 --> 19:59.750
Despa, there's a girl we 
wanna help with this money.

20:00.510 --> 20:02.310
What are you talking about?

20:02.310 --> 20:05.450
There's this girl that has a sick mother.

20:05.450 --> 20:08.810
If we give her that money, 
she may still pull through.

20:08.810 --> 20:11.930
But if we do that, it won't 
really solve anything.

20:12.280 --> 20:14.390
Despa, we need your help.

20:18.940 --> 20:24.430
Just as I was hoping. It looks like you 
really did learn your social lesson.

20:25.670 --> 20:27.670
Hm? Hmm?

20:27.670 --> 20:32.350
Don't tell me you thought 
I only wanted the money.

20:32.350 --> 20:37.210
What do you take me for? You let 
me handle things from here.

20:37.210 --> 20:38.620
Do you mean it?!

20:39.780 --> 20:43.380
Hmm? There's something funny here.

20:43.380 --> 20:48.230
There's no way Despa would do anything 
that didn't get him any money so easily.

20:48.640 --> 20:50.120
Of course not!

20:51.180 --> 20:53.640
So how about we do this?

20:54.290 --> 20:59.520
This is an investment in the future. 
I will teach her some lessons,

20:59.520 --> 21:02.500
and lend them the money they 
need, a little at a time.

21:02.890 --> 21:05.840
She'll attend to her studies, 
and by broadening her horizons,

21:05.840 --> 21:09.320
she will gain the knowledge 
it takes to make money. Then,

21:09.560 --> 21:12.280
once she's able to earn some money,

21:12.660 --> 21:15.730
I'll have her pay all of my money back.
